   "skos:definition": "The ideas about what wisdom is, who is wise and how wisdom grows that ordinary people carry around, usually without having spelled them out; psychologists study them by asking laypeople to describe, rate or nominate wise people, and contrast them with the explicit theories built by researchers.",
