   "skos:definition": "American psychologist (Yale, Tufts, Oklahoma State, Cornell) best known for his work on intelligence, creativity and love, who helped launch the psychology of wisdom by studying people's implicit theories of it and proposed the balance theory, which treats wisdom as using one's abilities for a common good.",
