   "rdfs:label": "Socratic ignorance",
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "Socrates' disavowal of knowledge",
    "Socratic wisdom",
    "human wisdom",
    "knowing that one does not know"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "wg:wisdom"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The teaching, drawn from Plato's Apology, that the beginning of human wisdom is not thinking you know what you do not know: an honest awareness of the limits of your own understanding, especially about the most important questions of how to live.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
